        {
         "@type": "meaningComprehension",
         "comprehends": [
          "copies/gs573tj9547.jsonld#inscription-text"
         ],
         "note": "Ink, upper panel upright: the number at the left, the date in the middle, one name to the right and a second below it. Every figure of the date is plain. Wössler is the hand already known from this corpus; the name above it I read as Hohmüller, though the minims after Hohm- could as well give Hohmüler and I cannot be sure of the umlaut."
        }
       ]
      }
     }
